{
  "body" : "CONTENT BRIEF\nCreate an illustration of {{subject}} in {{setting}}, shown {{pose}}. Keep the scene focused on the character and use only a few supporting background forms. Add a small handwritten artist signature: \"{{signature}}\". Additional constraints: {{extra}}\n\nSTYLE DIRECTION\nUse the reference balance of thick, irregular black contour lines, simplified cartoon anatomy, and broad, hard-edged cel-shaded color blocks. Build the image from clean, flat fills with sparse interior strokes and a few angular shadow shapes; retain slight hand-drawn unevenness rather than polished vector perfection. Use a mostly black and charcoal ground with cool gray secondary areas, pale warm cream skin or focal fills, and only tiny muted warm accents. Keep saturation low except for those small accents. Use crisp, high-contrast outlines and distinct overlaps to separate forms; shadows are solid graphic shapes, not soft gradients. {{style_adjustment}}\n\nDESIGN RULES\nPortrait 2:3 composition. Place one large, readable character centrally in the lower and middle frame, with the head as the main focal point and substantial dark negative space above. Keep the figure cropped by the lower frame and let broad, simple background bands sit behind it without competing with the silhouette. Preserve this scale, upper negative space, and strong foreground/background separation when the subject or setting changes.\n\nAVOID\nAvoid photorealistic rendering, delicate hairline outlines, smooth airbrushed gradients, glossy highlights, saturated multicolor palettes, dense scenery, and tiny decorative detail that weakens the bold silhouette.\n\nVARIABLES\nSubject: {{subject}}; setting: {{setting}}; pose: {{pose}}; style adjustment: {{style_adjustment}}; extra: {{extra}}.",
  "community" : {
    "author" : {
      "name" : "Gavin Schnee",
